# (auto-translated)
#: ../hacks/config/sphereeversion.xml.h:43
msgid ""
"\n"
"Turns a sphere inside out: a smooth deformation (homotopy).  During the\n"
"eversion, the deformed sphere is allowed to intersect itself transversally,\n"
"however, no creases or pinch points occur.\n"
"\n"
"Inspired by the following paper: Adam Bednorz, Witold Bednorz:\n"
"\"Analytic sphere eversion using ruled surfaces\", Differential Geometry\n"
"and its Applications 64:59-79, 2019.\n"
"\n"
"Also by the video \"Outside In\" by The Geometry Center (Bill Thurston, "
"Silvio\n"
"Levy, Delle Maxwell, Tamara Munzner, Nathaniel Thurston, David Ben-Zvi, "
"Matt\n"
"Headrick, et al.), 1994, and the accompanying booklet Silvio Levy: \"Making\n"
"Waves — A Guide to the Ideas Behind Outside In\", A K Peters, Wellesley, "
"MA,\n"
"1995.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphere_eversion\n"
"\n"
"Written by Carsten Steger; 2020.\n"
"  "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Stülpt eine Kugel um: eine sanfte Verformung (Homotopie).  Während der\n"
"Umstülpung, die verformte Kugel darf sich transversal schneiden,\n"
"Es treten jedoch keine Falten oder Quetschstellen auf.\n"
"\n"
"und seine Anwendungen 64:59-79, 2019.Inspiriert durch den folgenden Artikel: "
"Adam Bednorz, Witold Bednorz:\n"
"„Analytische Kugelumkehr unter Verwendung Regelflächen“, "
"Differentialgeometrie\n"
"\n"
"Auch im Video „Outside In“ von The Geometry Center (Bill Thurston, Silvio\n"
"Levy, Delle Maxwell, Tamara Munzner, Nathaniel Thurston, David Ben-Zvi, "
"Matt\n"
"Headrick, et al.), 1994, und die Begleitbroschüre Silvio Levy: „Making\n"
"Waves – Ein Leitfaden zu den Ideen hinter Outside In“, A K Peters, "
"Wellesley, MA,\n"
"1995.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphere_eversion\n"
"\n"
"Geschrieben von Carsten Steger; 2020.\n"
"  "

#: ../hacks/config/spheremonics.xml.h:1
msgid "Spheremonics"
msgstr "Spähremonie"

# (auto-translated)
#: ../hacks/config/spheremonics.xml.h:18
msgid "Smoothed lines"
msgstr "Geglättete Linien"

# (auto-translated)
#: ../hacks/config/spheremonics.xml.h:23
msgid ""
"\n"
"These closed objects are commonly called spherical harmonics,\n"
"although they are only remotely related to the mathematical\n"
"definition found in the solution to certain wave functions, most\n"
"notably the eigenfunctions of angular momentum operators.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Spherical_harmonics#Visualization_of_the_spherical_harmonics\n"
"\n"
"Written by Paul Bourke and Jamie Zawinski; 2002.\n"
"  "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Diese geschlossenen Objekte werden allgemein als sphärische Harmonische "
"bezeichnet.\n"
"obwohl sie nur entfernt mit dem Mathematischen verwandt sind\n"
"Die meisten Definitionen finden sich in der Lösung bestimmter "
"Wellenfunktionen\n"
"insbesondere die Eigenfunktionen von Drehimpulsoperatoren.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Spherical_harmonics#Visualization_of_the_spherical_harmonics\n"
"\n"
"Geschrieben von Paul Bourke und Jamie Zawinski; 2002.\n"
"  "

